# Real-time audio thread (`processBlock` / `renderNextBlock` / `ThreeLayerDrum::next`)

| Rule | Requirement |
|------|-------------|
| Heap | No `new`/`delete`/`malloc`, `vector::push_back`, `std::string`, `juce::String` in audio callbacks |
| Locks / I/O | No mutex, `CriticalSection`, file I/O, `DBG`, network in `processBlock` |
| UI | License verify, WAV load, clipboard — **message thread only** |
| Host data | `std::atomic` + `memory_order_relaxed` for flags; `SmoothedValue` for continuous params |
| Meters | `AbstractFifo` or SPSC to UI — never block audio thread |
| Denormals | `juce::ScopedNoDenormals` at top of `processBlock` |
| MIDI | Sample-accurate: split blocks at `MidiBuffer` event positions |

**Offline only:** `renderDesign()`, kit export, file writers — may allocate.

---

# Architecture

- **C++20:** `std::span`, `constexpr`, RAII; `unique_ptr` for non-RT ownership.
- **DSP separation:** Voices/oscillators/filters in testable units with `prepare(ProcessSpec)`, `reset()`, `process()` — not monolithic processors.
- **APVTS:** All automatable params; versioned `getStateInformation` / `setStateInformation` (max 1 MiB chunks — Strix-hardened parsers).
- **CMake only:** No `.jucer`; JUCE at `starter-cpp/externals/JUCE`.

